msgid "API reference"
msgstr "API 参考"

msgid ""
"The public functions take one-dimensional array-like inputs, such as lists, NumPy arrays or "
"pandas Series, and return NumPy arrays or pandas DataFrames. Import them from their modules."
msgstr "公共函数接收一维类数组输入（如列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series），返回 NumPy 数组或 pandas DataFrame。请从各自所在的模块导入。"

msgid ":py:obj:`binning.bin_edges <kivi.binning.bin_edges>`\\ \\(values\\[\\, bins\\, method\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`binning.bin_edges <kivi.binning.bin_edges>`\\ \\(values\\[\\, bins\\, method\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit numeric bin edges on a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合数值变量的分箱边界。"

msgid ":py:obj:`binning.cut <kivi.binning.cut>`\\ \\(values\\, edges\\, \\*\\[\\, special\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`binning.cut <kivi.binning.cut>`\\ \\(values\\, edges\\, \\*\\[\\, special\\]\\)"

msgid "Assign values to bins, with a separate group for each special value."
msgstr "将取值分配到各箱，每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe.woe_table <kivi.woe.woe_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, smoothing\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe.woe_table <kivi.woe.woe_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, smoothing\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute weight of evidence and information value for observed groups."
msgstr "按观察到的分组计算证据权重（WOE）和信息值（IV）。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`evaluate.psi_table <kivi.evaluate.psi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`evaluate.psi_table <kivi.evaluate.psi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compare two samples using their population stability index."
msgstr "通过群体稳定性指标（PSI）比较两个样本的分布。"

msgid ":py:obj:`datasets.Dataset.bank_data <kivi.datasets.Dataset.bank_data>`\\ \\(\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`datasets.Dataset.bank_data <kivi.datasets.Dataset.bank_data>`\\ \\(\\)"

msgid "Load 4,521 observations from UCI Bank Marketing."
msgstr "读取 UCI Bank Marketing 的 4,521 条营销记录。"

msgid "Binning"
msgstr "分箱"

msgid ""
"The edges are fitted once and then applied with ``pandas.cut`` to the reference and to every "
"sample compared with it."
msgstr "边界只拟合一次，然后用 ``pandas.cut`` 应用到基准样本以及每个与之比较的样本上。"

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "参数"

msgid "**values**"
msgstr "**values**"

msgid "array_like"
msgstr "array_like"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional numeric reference values, such as a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. "
"Missing values are omitted."
msgstr "一维数值型基准取值，可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。拟合时忽略缺失值。"

msgid "**bins**"
msgstr "**bins**"

msgid "int, default 5"
msgstr "int，默认 5"

msgid "Requested number of bins. Tied quantiles can reduce this number."
msgstr "期望箱数。分位点重合时实际箱数可能减少。"

msgid "**method**"
msgstr "**method**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"quantile\", \"uniform\"}, default \"quantile\""
msgstr "{\"quantile\", \"uniform\"}，默认 \"quantile\""

msgid "Use sample quantiles or equally spaced edges."
msgstr "使用样本分位点或等距边界。"

msgid "**special**"
msgstr "**special**"

msgid "array_like, optional"
msgstr "array_like，可选"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted when the edges are fitted."
" Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码，拟合边界时会被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid "Returns"
msgstr "返回值"

msgid "numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "numpy.ndarray"

msgid "Increasing edges with infinite endpoints, suitable for pandas.cut."
msgstr "严格递增的边界数组，两端为负无穷和正无穷，可直接传给 pandas.cut。"

msgid "Raises"
msgstr "异常"

msgid "ValueError"
msgstr "ValueError"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is not a positive integer, `method` is not recognized, `values` is not one-dimensional "
"or not numeric, `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value, or the reference "
"has no observations or contains an infinite value apart from special values."
msgstr "如果 `bins` 不是正整数、 `method` 无法识别、 `values` 不是一维或不是数值、 `special` 不是一维或含有缺失值，或者除特殊值外基准样本没有观测值或含有无穷值。"

msgid "Warns"
msgstr "警告"

msgid "UserWarning"
msgstr "UserWarning"

msgid ""
"If tied edges leave fewer bins than requested, for example when a single value accounts for a "
"large share of the reference."
msgstr "如果边界重合导致实际箱数少于期望箱数，例如某个取值在基准样本中占比很大。"

msgid ":obj:`cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`cut`"

msgid ":obj:`pandas.cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`pandas.cut`"

msgid "Assign values to the bins defined by the edges."
msgstr "按边界把取值分配到各箱。"

msgid ":obj:`numpy.quantile`"
msgstr ":obj:`numpy.quantile`"

msgid "Compute the quantile edges."
msgstr "计算分位数边界。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_table`"

msgid "Weight of evidence of the resulting groups."
msgstr "计算所得分组的证据权重。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.evaluate.psi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.evaluate.psi_table`"

msgid "Stability of the resulting groups."
msgstr "计算所得分组的稳定性。"

msgid "Notes"
msgstr "说明"

msgid ""
"Quantile edges are the sample quantiles at equally spaced probabilities, computed with the "
"default linear interpolation of ``numpy.quantile``. Uniform edges divide the range from the "
"smallest to the largest value into equal widths."
msgstr "分位数边界是在等间距概率处取的样本分位数，使用 ``numpy.quantile`` 默认的线性插值计算。等距边界把从最小值到最大值的区间等分。"

msgid ""
"Repeated edges are merged, and the outer edges are replaced with infinities, so every finite "
"value falls into exactly one interval. The intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right."
msgstr "重复的边界会被合并，最外侧的两个边界替换为无穷，因此每个有限值都恰好落入一个区间。 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间为左开右闭。"

msgid "Examples"
msgstr "示例"

msgid "A special value is left out of the fit:"
msgstr "特殊值不参与拟合："

msgid "Without `special` the result is the same as ``pandas.cut(values, edges)``."
msgstr "不传 `special` 时，结果与 ``pandas.cut(values, edges)`` 相同。"

msgid "One-dimensional numeric values to assign. Missing values stay missing."
msgstr "待分箱的一维数值。缺失值保持缺失。"

msgid "**edges**"
msgstr "**edges**"

msgid "Increasing bin edges, usually from `bin_edges`."
msgstr "递增的分箱边界，通常来自 `bin_edges` 。"

msgid ""
"Special values that each form their own group instead of falling into an interval. Use the values"
" passed to `bin_edges`."
msgstr "每个特殊值单独成组，不落入任何区间。请使用传给 `bin_edges` 的同一组值。"

msgid "pandas.Series or pandas.Categorical"
msgstr "pandas.Series 或 pandas.Categorical"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups whose categories are the special values, in the order given, followed by the "
"intervals. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and name."
msgstr "分类型的分组结果，类别依次为按给定顺序排列的特殊值和各区间。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `values` is not one-dimensional or is not numeric apart from special values, `edges` does not "
"increase, or `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value."
msgstr "如果 `values` 不是一维或除特殊值外不是数值、 `edges` 不是递增的，或者 `special` 不是一维或含有缺失值。"

msgid ":obj:`bin_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`bin_edges`"

msgid "Fit the edges on a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合边界。"

msgid "Assign values to intervals only."
msgstr "只把取值分配到区间。"

msgid ""
"A special value is matched by equality, so ``-1`` and ``-1.0`` are the same code. Values outside "
"the edges become missing, as with ``pandas.cut``; the infinite outer edges of `bin_edges` avoid "
"this."
msgstr ""
"特殊值按相等关系匹配，因此 ``-1`` 和 ``-1.0`` 视为同一个编码。与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，超出边界的值会变为缺失； `bin_edges` "
"两端的无穷边界可以避免这种情况。"

msgid "Weight of evidence"
msgstr "证据权重"

msgid ""
"Each group's share of events is compared with its share of non-events. Sum the ``iv`` column for "
"the information value of the variable."
msgstr "比较每组在全部事件中的占比与在全部非事件中的占比。将 ``iv`` 列求和即得到该变量的信息值。"

msgid "**groups**"
msgstr "**groups**"

msgid "Pre-binned values or category labels. Missing values form a group."
msgstr "已分箱的数值或类别标签。缺失值独立成组。"

msgid "**target**"
msgstr "**target**"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `groups` and `target` are both pandas Series, they"
" must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `groups` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**smoothing**"
msgstr "**smoothing**"

msgid "float, default 0.5"
msgstr "float，默认 0.5"

msgid "Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating shares."
msgstr "计算占比时，用这个正数替代零计数。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame"

msgid ""
"Event and non-event counts, their within-class shares, WOE and IV per group. Sum the iv column "
"for the variable's information value."
msgstr "各组的事件数、非事件数、各自在所属类别中的占比，以及 WOE 和 IV。将 iv 列求和即得到该变量的信息值。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` does not "
"contain both 0 and 1 or has missing or other labels, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive."
msgstr "如果输入不是一维、索引或长度不一致、 `target` 没有同时包含 0 和 1 或含有缺失值及其他标签，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.bin_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.bin_edges`"

msgid "Fit edges for numeric variables."
msgstr "为数值变量拟合分箱边界。"

msgid "Compare the distribution of two samples."
msgstr "比较两个样本的分布。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`p_i` and :math:`q_i` be its shares of all events and of all non-"
"events. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 分别为其在全部事件和全部非事件中的占比。则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\,\\mathrm{WOE}_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{IV}_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\,\\mathrm{WOE}_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{IV}_i."

msgid ""
"Each zero count is replaced with `smoothing` before the shares are normalized, so every WOE is "
"finite. The ``non_event`` and ``event`` columns always report the observed counts."
msgstr "在归一化占比之前，每个零计数都会被替换为 `smoothing`，因此每个 WOE 都是有限值。 ``non_event`` 和 ``event`` 列始终报告实际观测到的计数。"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups, such as the result of `kivi.binning.cut` or ``pandas.cut``, follow the order "
"of their categories with missing values last. Other groups follow the order in which they first "
"appear. Categories that are never observed are omitted."
msgstr "分类型的分组（例如 `kivi.binning.cut` 或 ``pandas.cut`` 的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。其他分组按首次出现的次序排列。从未出现的类别不会列出。"

msgid "References"
msgstr "参考文献"

msgid ""
"N. Siddiqi, \"Credit Risk Scorecards: Developing and Implementing Intelligent Credit Scoring\", "
"Wiley, 2006."
msgstr ""
"N. Siddiqi, \"Credit Risk Scorecards: Developing and Implementing Intelligent Credit Scoring\", "
"Wiley, 2006."

msgid "[R86ef760ac44f-1]_"
msgstr "[R86ef760ac44f-1]_"

msgid "Population stability"
msgstr "群体稳定性"

msgid ""
"Each group's share of the current sample is compared with its share of the reference sample. Sum "
"the ``psi`` column for the index."
msgstr "比较每组在当前样本中的占比与在基准样本中的占比。将 ``psi`` 列求和即得到该指数。"

msgid "**reference, current**"
msgstr "**reference, current**"

msgid ""
"Labels or values binned using the same edges. Missing values and categories observed in only one "
"sample are included."
msgstr "类别标签或按相同边界分箱的数值。保留缺失值以及仅出现在一侧的类别。"

msgid ""
"Counts, normalized shares and the PSI contribution of each group. Sum the psi column for the "
"population stability index."
msgstr "各组的原始计数、归一化占比和 PSI 贡献。对 psi 列求和即得到总体 PSI。"

msgid "If either sample is empty or not one-dimensional, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive."
msgstr "如果任一样本为空或不是一维，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。"

msgid "Fit edges on the reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合分箱边界。"

msgid "Relate the groups to a binary target."
msgstr "将分组与二分类目标关联起来。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`q_i` be its share of the reference sample and :math:`p_i` its "
"share of the current sample. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`q_i` 为其在基准样本中的占比，:math:`p_i` 为其在当前样本中的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{PSI}_i = (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{PSI}_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{PSI}_i = (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{PSI}_i."

msgid ""
"Each zero count is replaced with `smoothing` before the shares are normalized, so a group "
"observed in only one sample has a finite contribution. The ``reference`` and ``current`` columns "
"always report the observed counts."
msgstr "在归一化占比之前，每个零计数都会被替换为 `smoothing`，因此只在一个样本中出现的组也有有限的贡献值。 ``reference`` 和 ``current`` 列始终报告实际观测到的计数。"

msgid ""
"If both samples are categorical with the same categories, rows follow the order of the categories"
" with missing values last. Otherwise they follow the order in which the groups first appear, in "
"the reference sample and then in the current sample."
msgstr "如果两个样本都是分类型且类别相同，各行按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。否则按分组首次出现的次序排列，先看基准样本，再看当前样本。"

msgid "[Rb40ea4e016bb-1]_"
msgstr "[Rb40ea4e016bb-1]_"

msgid "Example data"
msgstr "示例数据"

msgid "The ``y`` response of the original data is returned as the binary ``target`` column."
msgstr "原始数据中的响应列 ``y`` 以二分类的 ``target`` 列返回。"

msgid "Sixteen features and the integer target. A value of 1 indicates a term deposit subscription."
msgstr "返回 16 个特征和整数标签 target。1 表示客户认购了定期存款。"

msgid "Relate a feature to ``target``."
msgstr "将某个特征与 ``target`` 关联起来。"

msgid ""
"Bank Marketing by S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez (2014) is distributed under CC BY 4.0. The "
"bundled CSV was converted from the legacy workbook."
msgstr "Bank Marketing 由 S. Moro、P. Rita 和 P. Cortez 于 2014 年发布，按 CC BY 4.0 授权。随包 CSV 由旧版工作簿转换而来。"

msgid ""
"S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez, \"Bank Marketing\", UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2014. "
"https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306"
msgstr ""
"S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez, \"Bank Marketing\", UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2014. "
"https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306"

msgid "[Re446c00e8929-1]_"
msgstr "[Re446c00e8929-1]_"

msgid "Development"
msgstr "开发"

msgid "Set up"
msgstr "环境准备"

msgid "Clone the repository and install it in editable mode with the test and documentation dependencies."
msgstr "克隆仓库，以可编辑模式安装，并同时安装测试和文档依赖。"

msgid "Build and verify"
msgstr "构建与验证"

msgid ""
"The doctest builder runs every example in these pages and in the docstrings. The HTML build "
"writes English and simplified Chinese editions under docs/_build/html. API signatures come from "
"the installed package."
msgstr "doctest 构建器会运行本文档页面和 docstring 中的全部示例。HTML 构建会在 docs/_build/html 下生成英文和简体中文两套文档。API 签名从已安装的包提取。"

msgid "Translations"
msgstr "翻译"

msgid ""
"The Chinese edition is generated from ``docs/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/kivi.po``. Every paragraph "
"of the English pages and of the public docstrings is one entry in that file. ``python "
"docs/build.py`` stops when an entry is missing, fuzzy or no longer used."
msgstr ""
"中文版由 ``docs/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/kivi.po`` 生成。英文页面和公共 docstring "
"中的每个段落都对应该文件中的一个条目。如果有条目缺失、标记为 fuzzy 或已不再使用，``python docs/build.py`` 会停止构建。"

msgid "After changing English text:"
msgstr "修改英文内容后："

msgid ""
"Run ``python docs/build.py --update-po``. New strings are added with an empty translation, and "
"changed strings keep their old translation marked as fuzzy."
msgstr "运行 ``python docs/build.py --update-po``。新字符串以空译文加入，已修改的字符串保留旧译文并标记为 fuzzy。"

msgid "Translate the empty entries, review the fuzzy ones and delete their ``#, fuzzy`` line."
msgstr "翻译空条目，复核 fuzzy 条目并删除其 ``#, fuzzy`` 行。"

msgid "Run ``python docs/build.py`` again."
msgstr "再次运行 ``python docs/build.py``。"

msgid ""
"Both editions must keep the same page names, because the language switch links each page to its "
"counterpart."
msgstr "两种语言的页面名称必须保持一致，因为语言切换按钮会链接到另一语言中的同名页面。"

msgid "Publishing the documentation"
msgstr "发布文档"

msgid ""
"The ``Documentation`` workflow on GitHub Actions runs the tests and builds both editions for "
"every pull request. On the master branch it also publishes docs/_build/html to the gh-pages "
"branch, which serves https://gchensy.github.io/kivi/."
msgstr ""
"GitHub Actions 上的 ``Documentation`` 工作流会对每个拉取请求运行测试并构建两种语言的文档。在 master 分支上，它还会把 docs/_build/html "
"发布到 gh-pages 分支，通过 https://gchensy.github.io/kivi/ 访问。"

msgid "Releasing to PyPI"
msgstr "发布到 PyPI"

msgid ""
"The ``Release`` workflow publishes kivi to PyPI when a GitHub release is published. It uses PyPI "
"trusted publishing, so no API token is stored in the repository."
msgstr ""
"发布 GitHub release 时，``Release`` 工作流会把 kivi 发布到 PyPI。它使用 PyPI 可信发布（trusted publishing），因此仓库中不保存任何 "
"API 令牌。"

msgid ""
"Set ``version`` in ``pyproject.toml`` to the new version, for example ``0.3.0``, and update "
":doc:`/release/index`."
msgstr "把 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的 ``version`` 改为新版本号，例如 ``0.3.0``，并更新 :doc:`/release/index`。"

msgid "Merge the change into the master branch."
msgstr "将改动合并到 master 分支。"

msgid "Publish a GitHub release whose tag is ``v`` followed by the version, for example ``v0.3.0``."
msgstr "发布一个 GitHub release，其标签为 ``v`` 加版本号，例如 ``v0.3.0``。"

msgid ""
"The workflow stops if the tag does not match the version. Otherwise it runs the tests, builds the"
" source distribution and the wheel, checks them with twine and uploads them."
msgstr "如果标签与版本号不一致，工作流会停止。否则它会运行测试，构建源码包和 wheel，用 twine 检查后上传。"

msgid ""
"Trusted publishing needs a one-time setup by an owner of the PyPI project: in the project's "
"publishing settings, add a GitHub publisher for the repository ``gchensy/kivi`` with the workflow"
" ``release.yml`` and the environment ``pypi``."
msgstr ""
"可信发布需要 PyPI 项目的所有者完成一次性设置：在项目的发布设置中添加一个 GitHub 发布者，仓库为 ``gchensy/kivi``，工作流为 ``release.yml``，环境为 "
"``pypi``。"

msgid "Legacy review"
msgstr "旧版评审"

msgid "Findings from the legacy implementation"
msgstr "旧版实现中的问题"

msgid ""
"Packaging. The 0.2.8 wheel placed NumPy and pandas behind the all extra. A default installation "
"could import kivi but failed on its dataset and WOE entry points."
msgstr "打包。0.2.8 的 wheel 将 NumPy 和 pandas 列在 all 可选依赖中。默认安装后可以导入 kivi，但加载数据和调用 WOE 都会失败。"

msgid ""
"Dependencies. evaluate/BucketsUtils.py imported PySpark at module load even for pandas PSI. Its "
"standalone CSI function also referenced an undefined self. The new metric functions depend on "
"pandas and NumPy."
msgstr ""
"依赖。evaluate/BucketsUtils.py 在模块加载时导入 PySpark，连 pandas 版 PSI 也依赖 Spark。该文件的独立 CSI 函数引用了未定义的 "
"self。新版指标函数只依赖 pandas 和 NumPy。"

msgid ""
"Numerical results. The old WOE zero-cell logic adjusted one class with an if/elif and used the "
"original totals. The old PSI helper modified the displayed counts. Tests now check raw counts, "
"normalized shares and hand-calculated metrics."
msgstr "数值结果。旧版 WOE 使用 if/elif 处理零频数，一次只调整一类，还沿用调整前的分母。旧版 PSI 会更改展示的计数。新版测试检查原始计数、归一化占比及手算指标。"

msgid ""
"State. Model/Tree.py removed the target column from the caller's frame. Dataset generation also "
"reset NumPy's global random state. Future estimators should preserve inputs and take a local "
"random seed."
msgstr "状态。Model/Tree.py 会从调用方传入的 DataFrame 中移除目标列。模拟数据生成器也会重置 NumPy 的全局随机状态。后续迁移估计器时，应保留输入并使用局部随机种子。"

msgid ""
"Coverage. Legacy scorecard and WOE tests printed tables without asserting the expected numbers. "
"Use frozen datasets to check fitted boundaries, score direction, special values and row counts "
"before porting these workflows."
msgstr "测试。旧版评分卡与 WOE 用例打印结果表，却没有断言具体数值。迁移前应用固定样本核对分箱边界、评分方向、特殊值和总行数。"

msgid ""
"Project scope. The former source tree mixed modeling, databases, distributed execution, notebooks"
" and deployment configuration. Keep infrastructure-specific imports inside optional integrations "
"and keep business SQL and local configuration outside the distribution."
msgstr "项目范围。旧目录混合了建模算法、数据库、分布式计算、笔记本与部署配置。新增集成时应在可选模块内导入相应依赖，将业务 SQL 和本地配置保留在分发包之外。"

msgid "Migration order"
msgstr "迁移顺序"

msgid ""
"Start with a fixed scorecard example. Compare old and new WOE on the same labeled rows, then "
"validate score transformation and model evaluation against stored outputs. Port weighted or "
"supervised binning next when a workflow requires it. Restore Spark and SQL independently after "
"the core inputs and outputs are stable."
msgstr "先固定一份评分卡样本，在相同标签和分箱上比较新旧 WOE，再用存档结果验证评分转换与模型评估。按业务需要迁移加权或监督分箱。核心输入输出稳定后，再分别接入 Spark 和 SQL。"

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "快速开始"

msgid ""
"kivi needs Python 3.10 or newer with NumPy and pandas. Install it, then follow the quickstart to "
"bin a variable, compute its weight of evidence and check its stability between two samples."
msgstr "kivi 需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本，以及 NumPy 和 pandas。安装后，可按快速上手完成一个变量的分箱、计算其证据权重，并检查它在两个样本之间的稳定性。"

msgid "Installation"
msgstr "安装"

msgid "Install from GitHub or a local checkout and check the version."
msgstr "从 GitHub 或本地仓库安装，并检查版本。"

msgid "Quickstart"
msgstr "快速上手"

msgid "A complete analysis of the bundled bank marketing data, with the output of every step."
msgstr "用随包的银行营销数据完成一次完整分析，并展示每一步的输出。"

msgid ""
"kivi requires Python 3.10 or newer, NumPy 1.24 or newer and pandas 2.0 or newer. pip installs "
"NumPy and pandas automatically."
msgstr "kivi 需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本、NumPy 1.24 或更高版本，以及 pandas 2.0 或更高版本。pip 会自动安装 NumPy 和 pandas。"

msgid "PyPI"
msgstr "PyPI"

msgid "Install the latest release:"
msgstr "安装最新发布版本："

msgid "GitHub"
msgstr "GitHub"

msgid "Install the development version directly from the repository:"
msgstr "直接从仓库安装开发版："

msgid "Local checkout"
msgstr "本地仓库"

msgid "Clone the repository and install it from the checkout:"
msgstr "克隆仓库后从本地安装："

msgid "Check the installed version:"
msgstr "检查已安装的版本："

msgid ""
"To work on kivi itself, use an editable install with the test and documentation dependencies. See"
" :doc:`/development/index`."
msgstr "如需参与 kivi 开发，请使用可编辑安装并加装测试和文档依赖，详见 :doc:`/development/index`。"

msgid ""
"The 0.2.x releases have a different API. Read :doc:`/release/migration` before upgrading existing"
" code."
msgstr "0.2.x 版本的 API 与当前版本不同。升级已有代码前，请先阅读 :doc:`/release/migration`。"

msgid ""
"This walkthrough bins a numeric and a categorical variable from the bundled data, measures how "
"well each bin separates the target and checks whether the age distribution shifts between two "
"samples. Every output below is produced by the code above it."
msgstr "本教程对随包数据中的一个数值变量和一个类别变量进行分箱，衡量各箱对目标的区分能力，并检查年龄分布在两个样本之间是否发生偏移。下面的每个输出都由其上方的代码生成。"

msgid "Load the data"
msgstr "加载数据"

msgid ""
"The bundled bank marketing data records whether a customer subscribed to a term deposit. The "
"split below demonstrates two samples; the rows do not represent a chronological validation split."
msgstr "随包的营销数据记录了客户是否认购定期存款。下面按行切出两个样本演示用法，这一切分没有时间验证含义。"

msgid "Fit bins on the reference sample"
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合分箱"

msgid ""
"Fit the edges on the reference sample only, then reuse them for every other sample so that the "
"counts remain comparable."
msgstr "只在基准样本上拟合边界，再将同一组边界用于其他所有样本，使各组计数保持可比。"

msgid ""
"The outer edges are infinite, so an age outside the reference range still falls into the first or"
" last bin."
msgstr "最外侧的边界为无穷，因此超出基准范围的年龄仍会落入第一个或最后一个箱。"

msgid "``woe_table`` returns one row per bin, in the order of the intervals."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 每箱返回一行，按区间顺序排列。"

msgid ""
"A positive WOE means that the bin holds a larger share of the subscribers than of the non-"
"subscribers. Age on its own separates the two groups only weakly."
msgstr "WOE 为正表示该箱在认购客户中的占比高于在未认购客户中的占比。仅凭年龄区分这两类客户的能力较弱。"

msgid ""
"Read the per-bin contributions before interpreting a total. A group with few events can have a "
"large WOE despite representing few customers."
msgstr "解读总值前先检查每一箱的贡献。只有少量事件的箱也可能有很大的 WOE，但它代表的客户可能很少。"

msgid "Categorical variables"
msgstr "类别变量"

msgid "Pass category labels directly; they need no edges."
msgstr "类别标签可以直接传入，无需边界。"

msgid "``psi_table`` compares the two samples bin by bin. It does not use the target."
msgstr "``psi_table`` 逐箱比较两个样本，不使用目标标签。"

msgid "Next steps"
msgstr "后续阅读"

msgid ""
":doc:`/user_guide/binning` explains quantile and uniform edges, ties, special values and missing "
"values."
msgstr ":doc:`/user_guide/binning` 介绍等频与等距边界、重复切点、特殊值和缺失值。"

msgid ":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` and :doc:`/user_guide/psi` give the formulas and the smoothing rule."
msgstr ":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 和 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 给出计算公式与平滑规则。"

msgid ":doc:`/api` lists every parameter."
msgstr ":doc:`/api` 列出全部参数。"

msgid "Binning, WOE, IV and PSI for pandas"
msgstr "基于 pandas 的分箱、WOE、IV 与 PSI"

msgid ""
"kivi fits bin edges on a reference sample, measures how well each bin separates a binary target "
"and tracks how the population shifts over time. Every result is a pandas DataFrame with one row "
"per bin."
msgstr "kivi 在基准样本上拟合分箱边界，衡量每一箱对二分类目标的区分能力，并跟踪样本分布随时间的变化。所有结果都是每箱一行的 pandas DataFrame。"

msgid "At a glance"
msgstr "速览"

msgid "How it works"
msgstr "工作流程"

msgid "Fit edges once"
msgstr "拟合一次边界"

msgid ""
"Call ``bin_edges`` on the reference sample. The outer edges are infinite, so later values always "
"fall into a bin."
msgstr "在基准样本上调用 ``bin_edges``。最外侧边界为无穷，因此后续数据总能落入某个箱。"

msgid "Cut every sample"
msgstr "对每个样本分箱"

msgid ""
"Apply the saved edges with ``pandas.cut``. Categorical columns skip this step and are passed as "
"they are."
msgstr "用保存的边界调用 ``pandas.cut``。类别变量跳过这一步，直接传入原始标签。"

msgid "Measure"
msgstr "计算指标"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` scores each bin against the target and ``psi_table`` compares two samples. Sum a "
"column for the total."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 按目标评估每一箱，``psi_table`` 比较两个样本。对相应列求和即得到总值。"

msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "文档"

msgid "Install kivi and walk through a complete analysis of the bundled bank marketing data."
msgstr "安装 kivi，并用随包的银行营销数据完成一次完整分析。"

msgid "User guide"
msgstr "用户指南"

msgid "How bins are fitted and how WOE, IV and PSI are defined, including missing values and smoothing."
msgstr "分箱边界如何拟合，WOE、IV 和 PSI 如何定义，以及缺失值与平滑的处理方式。"

msgid "Parameters, return values and examples for every public function."
msgstr "每个公共函数的参数、返回值和示例。"

msgid "Release notes"
msgstr "版本说明"

msgid "What changed in 0.3 and how to migrate code written for 0.2.x."
msgstr "0.3 的变化，以及如何迁移为 0.2.x 编写的代码。"

msgid "Unreleased"
msgstr "未发布"

msgid "New"
msgstr "新增"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` takes a ``special`` argument. Codes such as ``-1`` or ``-999`` are left out when "
"the edges are fitted."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 新增 ``special`` 参数。 ``-1`` 、 ``-999`` 等编码在拟合边界时会被排除。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.binning.cut`` assigns values to the fitted bins and gives each special value its own "
"group. Without special values it returns the same result as ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr "``kivi.binning.cut`` 把取值分配到拟合好的各箱，并让每个特殊值单独成组。不传特殊值时，结果与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid "Changed"
msgstr "变更"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges``, ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` accept any one-dimensional array-like input, such "
"as a list or a NumPy array. Group and target series passed to ``woe_table`` must still share an "
"index; arrays and lists are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 、 ``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 接受任意一维类数组输入，例如列表或 NumPy 数组。传给 ``woe_table`` "
"的分组与标签序列仍须共享同一索引；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` issues a ``UserWarning`` when tied edges leave fewer bins than requested. The "
"message names the most frequent value so that it can be passed in ``special``."
msgstr "边界重合导致实际箱数少于期望箱数时， ``bin_edges`` 会发出 ``UserWarning`` 。提示信息会写出出现次数最多的取值，便于将其传给 ``special`` 。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` list categorical groups, including the result of ``pandas.cut``, "
"in category order with missing values last. Other labels keep the order in which they first "
"appear. Previously all groups followed first appearance, and ``sort_index`` was needed to put "
"intervals in order."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 对分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` "
"的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。其他标签仍按首次出现的次序排列。此前所有分组都按首次出现的次序排列，需要用 ``sort_index`` 才能让区间有序。"

msgid "Error messages name the argument and report the value received."
msgstr "错误信息会写明参数名以及收到的值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.__version__`` is ``\"0+unknown\"`` when kivi is imported from a source tree that is not "
"installed, instead of raising an error."
msgstr "从未安装的源码目录导入 kivi 时， ``kivi.__version__`` 为 ``\"0+unknown\"`` ，不再抛出错误。"

msgid "Group counts use ``numpy.bincount``, which is faster on large samples."
msgstr "分组计数改用 ``numpy.bincount`` ，在大样本上更快。"

msgid "The API reference documents errors, warnings, formulas and related functions."
msgstr "API 参考补充了异常、警告、公式和相关函数的说明。"

msgid "0.3.0 (2026-11-19)"
msgstr "0.3.0（2026-11-19）"

msgid ""
"A rewrite around a small pandas core. Read :doc:`migration` before upgrading code written for "
"0.2.x."
msgstr "围绕精简的 pandas 核心重写。升级为 0.2.x 编写的代码前，请先阅读 :doc:`migration`。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` fits quantile or uniform edges on a reference sample. The outer edges are infinite,"
" so the result can be passed to ``pandas.cut`` for any later sample."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合等频或等距边界。最外侧边界为无穷，因此结果可以传给 ``pandas.cut``，用于之后的任意样本。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` return raw counts, smoothed shares and a contribution for each "
"group, including missing values."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 返回每组的原始计数、平滑后的占比和单组贡献，缺失值也单独成组。"

msgid "Documentation in English and Simplified Chinese."
msgstr "提供英文和简体中文文档。"

msgid "NumPy and pandas are required dependencies. The 0.2.8 wheel placed them behind the ``all`` extra."
msgstr "NumPy 和 pandas 成为必需依赖。0.2.8 的 wheel 曾将它们放在 ``all`` 可选依赖中。"

msgid "The ``psi`` column holds the contribution of each bin. It previously repeated the overall total."
msgstr "``psi`` 列给出每箱的贡献，此前该列逐行重复总值。"

msgid ""
"Zero counts are replaced before each distribution is normalized, and reported counts are no "
"longer modified."
msgstr "先替换零计数，再分别对各分布归一化；结果中的计数不再被修改。"

msgid "Removed"
msgstr "移除"

msgid ""
"Spark, SQL, AHP, feature selection, model wrappers, weighted and supervised binning and "
"scorecards. They remain in the repository history."
msgstr "Spark、SQL、AHP、特征选择、模型封装、加权与监督分箱以及评分卡。这些代码仍保留在仓库历史中。"

msgid "Migrating from 0.2.x"
msgstr "从 0.2.x 迁移"

msgid ""
"The functions below replace the 0.2.x classes. Dataset.bank_data() retains its import path and "
"table schema. The target describes deposit subscription."
msgstr "下表列出取代 0.2.x 各个类的函数。Dataset.bank_data() 保留原有的导入路径和表结构，标签表示客户是否认购定期存款。"

msgid "0.2.x"
msgstr "0.2.x"

msgid "0.3"
msgstr "0.3"

msgid "``DistanceBins``"
msgstr "``DistanceBins``"

msgid "``bin_edges(values, method=\"uniform\")``, then ``pandas.cut`` and ``woe_table``"
msgstr "``bin_edges(values, method=\"uniform\")``，然后调用 ``pandas.cut`` 和 ``woe_table``"

msgid "``FrequencyBins``"
msgstr "``FrequencyBins``"

msgid "``bin_edges(values, method=\"quantile\")``, then ``pandas.cut`` and ``woe_table``"
msgstr "``bin_edges(values, method=\"quantile\")``，然后调用 ``pandas.cut`` 和 ``woe_table``"

msgid "``abnormal_vals=[...]``"
msgstr "``abnormal_vals=[...]``"

msgid "``special=[...]`` in ``bin_edges`` and ``kivi.binning.cut``"
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 和 ``kivi.binning.cut`` 的 ``special=[...]``"

msgid "``CategoryBins``"
msgstr "``CategoryBins``"

msgid "``woe_table(labels, target)``"
msgstr "``woe_table(labels, target)``"

msgid "``PSI.fit()``"
msgstr "``PSI.fit()``"

msgid "``psi_table(before, after)`` on groups formed with the same edges"
msgstr "对用同一组边界划分的分组调用 ``psi_table(before, after)``"

msgid "``Dataset.bank_data()``"
msgstr "``Dataset.bank_data()``"

msgid "Unchanged"
msgstr "不变"

msgid "Binning and WOE"
msgstr "分箱与 WOE"

msgid ""
"DistanceBins and FrequencyBins previously calculated group assignments and statistics together. "
"Use bin_edges with uniform or quantile, call pandas.cut, then pass the groups to woe_table. Codes"
" listed in abnormal_vals become the special argument: pass them to bin_edges, and use "
"kivi.binning.cut with the same codes in place of pandas.cut. CategoryBins users can pass the "
"label series directly."
msgstr ""
"旧版 DistanceBins 和 FrequencyBins 在同一步骤中完成分箱和统计。现在先用 bin_edges 选择 uniform 或 quantile，再用 pandas.cut "
"分组，最后将结果传给 woe_table。abnormal_vals 中的编码改由 special 参数指定：传给 bin_edges，并用带相同编码的 kivi.binning.cut 代替 "
"pandas.cut。原 CategoryBins 用户可直接传入类别标签序列。"

msgid ""
"For PSI.fit(), form both sets of groups using the same reference edges, then call psi_table. It "
"returns raw counts and a contribution per bin. Previously the psi column repeated the overall "
"total. The new smoothing rule preserves counts and normalizes each distribution after replacing "
"zeros. Recheck thresholds when migrating saved analyses."
msgstr ""
"迁移 PSI.fit() 时，先用同一组基准边界划分两期样本，再调用 psi_table。新结果包含各组的真实计数和单组贡献；旧结果在 psi "
"列逐行重复总值。新的平滑口径会在补零后归一化。迁移历史分析时应重新核对阈值。"

msgid "Not yet ported"
msgstr "尚未迁移的功能"

msgid ""
"Release 0.3 covers unweighted counts. Keep existing weighted, supervised binning and scorecard "
"workflows on their original version until their outputs have been validated on fixed reference "
"samples. Spark, SQL, AHP, feature selection, model wrappers and application code remain in the "
"historical revisions."
msgstr "0.3 版支持未加权统计。加权、监督分箱和评分卡流程应在固定样本上完成输出核对后再切换。历史版本中仍可查阅 Spark、SQL、AHP、特征选择、模型封装及应用代码。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` fits numeric bin edges on a reference sample and returns them as an array for "
"``pandas.cut``. The reference can be a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. Keep the array: "
"the same edges must be applied to every sample that is compared with the reference."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合数值分箱边界，并以数组形式返回，供 ``pandas.cut`` 使用。基准样本可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas "
"Series。请保存这个数组：与基准样本比较的每个样本都必须使用同一组边界。"

msgid "Quantile and uniform edges"
msgstr "等频与等距边界"

msgid ""
"Use quantile bins to divide the reference observations by rank, or uniform bins to divide their "
"numeric range into equal widths."
msgstr "等频分箱按基准样本中的秩划分观测，等距分箱按取值范围等宽划分。"

msgid ""
"Quantile bins hold roughly equal numbers of observations, which suits skewed variables. Uniform "
"bins keep equal widths, so a long tail can leave some bins nearly empty."
msgstr "等频分箱中各箱的观测数大致相同，适合偏态变量。等距分箱保持宽度一致，长尾可能让部分箱几乎为空。"

msgid "Ties and constant values"
msgstr "重复切点与常量"

msgid "Tied cut points are collapsed. A constant reference produces one bin."
msgstr "重复的切点会被合并。常量基准样本只产生一个箱。"

msgid ""
"The number of bins can therefore be smaller than requested, and ``bin_edges`` then issues a "
"``UserWarning``. A single value that covers much of the reference, such as a code for \"not "
"applicable\", often causes this. Pass that value in ``special``, as described in the next "
"section."
msgstr ""
"因此实际箱数可能少于期望箱数，此时 ``bin_edges`` 会发出 ``UserWarning`` "
"。某个取值（例如表示“不适用”的编码）在基准样本中占比很大时，常会出现这种情况。请按下一节的方法把该取值传给 ``special`` 。"

msgid "Special values"
msgstr "特殊值"

msgid ""
"Many credit variables use codes such as ``-1`` or ``-999`` for \"not applicable\" or \"no "
"record\". Such a code is not a measurement, so it should neither shape the edges nor share an "
"interval with real values. Pass the codes in ``special`` to ``bin_edges`` to leave them out of "
"the fit, and pass the same codes to ``kivi.binning.cut`` to give each one its own group."
msgstr ""
"许多信贷变量用 ``-1`` 或 ``-999`` 这样的编码表示“不适用”或“无记录”。这类编码不是测量值，既不应影响边界，也不应与真实取值共用一个区间。把这些编码传给 "
"``bin_edges`` 的 ``special`` 参数，拟合时会排除它们；再把同样的编码传给 ``kivi.binning.cut`` ，每个编码就会单独成组。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"In the bundled data, ``pdays`` is ``-1`` for the 82% of customers who were not contacted in an "
"earlier campaign. Without ``special``, every quantile is tied at ``-1``: ``bin_edges`` returns a "
"single bin and warns that ``-1`` makes up 82% of the fitted values. With ``special=[-1]`` the "
"remaining values are divided into five bins:"
msgstr ""
"在随包数据中，82% 的客户此前未被联系过，他们的 ``pdays`` 为 ``-1`` 。不传 ``special`` 时，所有分位点都重合在 ``-1`` ： ``bin_edges`` "
"只返回一个箱，并警告 ``-1`` 占拟合取值的 82%。传入 ``special=[-1]`` 后，其余取值被分成五个箱："

msgid ""
"The single bin had an IV of zero; separating the code shows that ``pdays`` is informative. The "
"categories of the result are the special values in the order given, followed by the intervals, "
"and ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` list the rows in that order. Special values are matched by "
"equality, so ``-1`` and ``-1.0`` are the same code. Without ``special``, ``cut`` returns the same"
" result as ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr ""
"原来那唯一一个箱的 IV 为零；把编码单独分出来之后，可以看出 ``pdays`` 是有信息量的。结果的类别依次为按给定顺序排列的特殊值和各区间， ``woe_table`` 和 "
"``psi_table`` 也按这个顺序列出各行。特殊值按相等关系匹配，因此 ``-1`` 和 ``-1.0`` 视为同一个编码。不传 ``special`` 时， ``cut`` 的结果与 "
"``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid "Applying the edges"
msgstr "应用边界"

msgid ""
"Infinite endpoints cover finite future observations outside the training range. Use the saved "
"edges with pandas.cut on every sample."
msgstr "两端延伸至无穷，因此可覆盖后续超出训练范围的有限值。保存边界，再对每期数据调用 pandas.cut。"

msgid ""
"Intervals are closed on the right, so a value equal to an edge belongs to the lower bin. Pass "
"``labels=False`` to ``pandas.cut`` for integer bin numbers instead of intervals."
msgstr "区间为左开右闭，因此等于某个边界的值归入较低的箱。若要得到整数箱号而不是区间，可向 ``pandas.cut`` 传入 ``labels=False``。"

msgid "Missing values and categories"
msgstr "缺失值与类别"

msgid ""
"Missing reference values are ignored when the edges are fitted, and ``pandas.cut`` leaves them "
"missing. The metric functions then count them as a separate group."
msgstr "拟合边界时会忽略基准样本中的缺失值，``pandas.cut`` 也会保留缺失值。指标函数随后将它们计为单独的一组。"

msgid ""
"Pass categorical labels directly to the metric functions. A missing label is a separate group. "
"Only observed groups appear. Categorical groups, including the result of ``pandas.cut``, follow "
"the order of their categories with missing values last; other labels follow the order in which "
"they first appear. For WOE, group and target series must have identical indices; arrays and lists"
" are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"类别变量可直接传给指标函数。缺失标签独立成组。输出仅列出实际观测到的组。分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` 的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后；其他标签按首次出现的次序排列。计算"
" WOE 时，分组与标签序列的索引必须完全一致；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid "Invalid input"
msgstr "无效输入"

msgid "``bin_edges`` raises ``ValueError`` when:"
msgstr "以下情况下，``bin_edges`` 会抛出 ``ValueError``："

msgid "``bins`` is not a positive integer;"
msgstr "``bins`` 不是正整数；"

msgid "``method`` is neither ``\"quantile\"`` nor ``\"uniform\"``;"
msgstr "``method`` 既不是 ``\"quantile\"`` 也不是 ``\"uniform\"``；"

msgid "the reference values are not one-dimensional or not numeric;"
msgstr "基准样本的取值不是一维或不是数值；"

msgid "``special`` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value;"
msgstr "``special`` 不是一维或含有缺失值；"

msgid ""
"the reference has no observations apart from missing and special values, or contains an infinite "
"value that is not special."
msgstr "除缺失值和特殊值外，基准样本没有观测值，或含有不属于特殊值的无穷值。"

msgid ""
"``Dataset.bank_data()`` loads 4,521 customers from the Bank Marketing data set. It has sixteen "
"features and an integer ``target``: 1 means that the customer subscribed to a term deposit."
msgstr ""
"``Dataset.bank_data()`` 读取 Bank Marketing 数据集中的 4,521 位客户。数据包含 16 个特征和整数标签 ``target``：1 "
"表示客户认购了定期存款。"

msgid ""
"The examples in this documentation split the rows by position only to demonstrate two samples; "
"the split is not chronological."
msgstr "本文档中的示例按行的位置切分出两个样本，仅用于演示；这一切分不代表时间顺序。"

msgid "Dataset and attribution"
msgstr "示例数据和署名"

msgid ""
"Bank Marketing by S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez (2014) is distributed under CC BY 4.0. The "
"bundled CSV was converted from the legacy workbook. The loader encodes subscription as 1 and non-"
"subscription as 0. See the `dataset record <https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306>`_ and `license "
"<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Bank Marketing 由 S. Moro、P. Rita 和 P. Cortez 于 2014 年发布，按 CC BY 4.0 授权。随包 CSV "
"由旧版工作簿转换而来。加载时将认购存款编码为 1，未认购编码为 0。详见 `数据集说明 <https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306>`_ 和 `许可证 "
"<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>`_。"

msgid ""
"Analyze a binary response and track changes in a population with pandas. Use the same bin edges "
"in development and monitoring so that counts remain comparable."
msgstr "使用 pandas 分析二分类标签并监测样本分布变化。在开发和监测阶段复用同一套分箱边界，可以直接比较各组计数。"

msgid ""
"kivi keeps fitting and measuring apart. ``bin_edges`` fits edges on a reference sample, "
"``pandas.cut`` assigns every sample to those bins, and ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` summarize "
"the resulting groups. The metric functions accept any grouping, so category labels can be passed "
"directly."
msgstr ""
"kivi 将拟合与计算分开。``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合边界，``pandas.cut`` 把每个样本划入这些箱，``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` "
"再汇总得到的分组。指标函数接受任意分组，因此类别标签可以直接传入。"

msgid ""
"Quantile and uniform edges, tied cut points, special values, values outside the reference range "
"and missing values."
msgstr "等频与等距边界、重复切点、特殊值、超出基准范围的值以及缺失值。"

msgid "Weight of evidence and information value"
msgstr "证据权重与信息值"

msgid "Definitions, the smoothing rule for empty cells and how to read the result."
msgstr "定义、空单元格的平滑规则以及结果的解读方法。"

msgid "Population stability index"
msgstr "群体稳定性指标"

msgid "Compare the distribution of two samples, including categories seen in only one of them."
msgstr "比较两个样本的分布，包括只在其中一个样本出现的类别。"

msgid "The bundled bank marketing data, its target and its license."
msgstr "随包的银行营销数据、其目标标签与许可证。"

msgid ""
"``psi_table`` compares the distribution of a variable in two samples, typically the development "
"sample and a later monitoring sample. Group both samples with the same edges or labels before "
"calling it."
msgstr "``psi_table`` 比较一个变量在两个样本中的分布，通常是开发样本和之后的监测样本。调用前，请用同一组边界或标签对两个样本分组。"

msgid "Definition"
msgstr "定义"

msgid ""
"Each contribution is zero or positive. PSI describes distribution change; it does not use the "
"outcome label."
msgstr "每一项贡献都大于或等于零。PSI 描述的是分布变化，不使用目标标签。"

msgid "Missing values and new categories"
msgstr "缺失值与新类别"

msgid ""
"Missing values form their own group, and categories appearing in only one sample are retained. "
"Their empty cells are smoothed exactly as in :doc:`woe_iv`, so every contribution stays finite."
msgstr "缺失值单独成组，只在一个样本中出现的类别也会保留。它们的空单元格按 :doc:`woe_iv` 中的方式平滑，因此每一项贡献都是有限值。"

msgid "Reading the result"
msgstr "解读结果"

msgid "Column"
msgstr "列"

msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "含义"

msgid "``reference``, ``current``"
msgstr "``reference``, ``current``"

msgid "Observed counts in each group."
msgstr "每组的实际观测数。"

msgid "``reference_share``, ``current_share``"
msgstr "``reference_share``, ``current_share``"

msgid ":math:`q_i` and :math:`p_i` after smoothing; each column sums to 1."
msgstr "平滑后的 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i`；每列之和为 1。"

msgid "``psi``"
msgstr "``psi``"

msgid "The group's contribution. Sum the column to obtain total drift."
msgstr "该组的贡献。对该列求和得到整体漂移。"

msgid ""
"A common convention reads a PSI below 0.1 as a small shift, 0.1 to 0.25 as a moderate shift and "
"above 0.25 as a large shift. The thresholds depend on the number of bins and on the smoothing "
"rule, so recheck them when moving analyses from 0.2.x."
msgstr "一种常见的经验口径是：PSI 低于 0.1 视为变化较小，0.1 到 0.25 为中等变化，高于 0.25 为显著变化。这些阈值取决于箱数和平滑规则，从 0.2.x 迁移分析时请重新核对。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` measures how each group separates a binary target. An event is target 1 and a non-"
"event is target 0. Both target classes must be present. Group and target series must share the "
"same index; arrays and lists are matched by position."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 衡量每组对二分类目标的区分能力。标签 1 表示事件，0 表示非事件。数据须同时包含两类标签。分组与标签序列的索引必须相同；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "定义"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`E_i` and :math:`N_i` be its numbers of events and non-events. Its"
" shares of all events and of all non-events are"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`E_i` 和 :math:`N_i` 分别为其事件数和非事件数。它在全部事件和全部非事件中的占比为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p_i = \\frac{E_i}{\\sum_j E_j}, \\qquad q_i = \\frac{N_i}{\\sum_j N_j}."
msgstr "p_i = \\frac{E_i}{\\sum_j E_j}, \\qquad q_i = \\frac{N_i}{\\sum_j N_j}."

msgid "The weight of evidence and the information value contribution of the group are"
msgstr "该组的证据权重和信息值贡献为"

msgid ""
"A positive WOE means that the group is relatively more common among events. Each IV contribution "
"is zero or positive, because :math:`p_i - q_i` and :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` always share a sign."
msgstr "WOE 为正表示该组在事件中相对更常见。每组的 IV 贡献都大于或等于零，因为 :math:`p_i - q_i` 与 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` 的符号始终相同。"

msgid "A worked example"
msgstr "计算示例"

msgid ""
"Two thirds of group ``a`` are events and two thirds of group ``b`` are non-events, so the two "
"groups have opposite WOE values of :math:`\\pm\\ln 2`."
msgstr "组 ``a`` 中三分之二是事件，组 ``b`` 中三分之二是非事件，因此两组的 WOE 互为相反数，等于 :math:`\\pm\\ln 2`。"

msgid "Smoothing empty cells"
msgstr "空单元格的平滑"

msgid ""
"A group without events or without non-events would have an infinite WOE. Before the shares are "
"computed, each zero count is replaced by the ``smoothing`` value :math:`s`:"
msgstr "没有事件或没有非事件的组，其 WOE 会是无穷。计算占比前，每个零计数都会被替换为 ``smoothing`` 参数值 :math:`s`："

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\tilde E_i = \\begin{cases} E_i & E_i > 0 \\\\ s & E_i = 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\tilde E_i}{\\sum_j \\tilde E_j},"
msgstr ""
"\\tilde E_i = \\begin{cases} E_i & E_i > 0 \\\\ s & E_i = 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad\n"
"p_i = \\frac{\\tilde E_i}{\\sum_j \\tilde E_j},"

msgid ""
"and likewise for non-events. Smoothing replaces zero cells with 0.5 by default. Each column is "
"then normalized separately. Counts in the result always report observations."
msgstr "非事件同理。平滑默认用 0.5 替换零频数，再按列分别归一化。结果表中的计数始终是实际观测数。"

msgid ""
"Changing smoothing can materially change the result for sparse bins. Merge small bins, or compare"
" several smoothing values, before relying on their WOE."
msgstr "修改平滑参数可能显著改变稀疏分箱的结果。在依赖这些箱的 WOE 之前，请合并小箱，或比较多个平滑取值的结果。"

msgid "``non_event``, ``event``"
msgstr "``non_event``, ``event``"

msgid "``non_event_share``, ``event_share``"
msgstr "``non_event_share``, ``event_share``"

msgid "``woe``"
msgstr "``woe``"

msgid ":math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`."
msgstr ":math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)`."

msgid "``iv``"
msgstr "``iv``"

msgid "The group's IV contribution. Sum the column for the variable's IV."
msgstr "该组的 IV 贡献。对该列求和得到变量的 IV。"

msgid ""
"A widely used rule of thumb reads an IV below 0.02 as not predictive, 0.02 to 0.1 as weak, 0.1 to"
" 0.3 as medium and above 0.3 as strong. Treat these bands as a starting point, not as a test; a "
"very high IV often points to a leak of the target into the variable."
msgstr ""
"一种广泛使用的经验口径是：IV 低于 0.02 视为无预测力，0.02 到 0.1 为弱，0.1 到 0.3 为中等，高于 0.3 为强。这些区间只是参考起点，而非检验标准；IV "
"过高往往意味着目标信息泄漏到了该变量中。"

